A segment cell focused
description: the cell_editing state
- >
  The clicked (or focused) cell holds the caret where the click put it; the append cell opens
  empty after the last segment. The TOC swaps to the live FILTER of the query the cells spell -
  matches and all their ancestors, expanded, no selection. Candidate and filter fetches are
  (re)scheduled on every text change
- !!<*yamlover: $defs: table>
  header:
    - Event
      width: 2
    - 'Condition / note'
      width: 4
    - 'Next state'
      width: 2
  - ['`alphanumeric`', '', '`cell_editing` (stays)']
  - ['`colon`', '(pick) the FIRST cell is empty - the scope ladder CLIMBS (bare → `:` → `::` → `:::`), the cells stay', '`cell_editing` (stays)']
  - ['`colon`', 'otherwise - the cell splits at the caret', '`cell_editing` (stays)']
  - ['`open_bracket`', 'the cell is empty and a previous segment exists - the index folds into it, caret inside the projected pair', '[index_editing](*::server:query-editor:index_editing)']
  - ['`open_bracket`', 'otherwise - the pair is projected at the caret', '[index_editing](*::server:query-editor:index_editing)']
  - ['`candidates_arrive`', '', '[dropdown_open](*::server:query-editor:dropdown_open)']
  - ['`backspace`', 'the caret sits inside an empty projected `[]` - the pair dismantles', '`cell_editing` (stays)']
  - ['`backspace`', 'the caret is at the cell''s start and a previous cell exists - the `:` boundary deletes, cells merge at the junction', '`cell_editing` (stays)']
  - ['`backspace`', '(pick) the caret is at the FIRST cell''s start and the ladder is above bare - the ladder steps DOWN', '`cell_editing` (stays)']
  - ['`backspace`', 'otherwise', '`cell_editing` (stays)']
  - ['`delete`', 'the caret is at the cell''s end and a next cell exists - the `:` boundary deletes, cells merge', '`cell_editing` (stays)']
  - ['`delete`', 'otherwise', '`cell_editing` (stays)']
  - ['`left_arrow`', 'the caret is at the cell''s start', '[focus_prev](*::server:query-editor:focus_prev)']
  - ['`left_arrow`', 'otherwise', '`cell_editing` (stays)']
  - ['`right_arrow`', 'the caret is at the cell''s end', '[focus_next](*::server:query-editor:focus_next)']
  - ['`right_arrow`', 'otherwise', '`cell_editing` (stays)']
  - ['`enter`', '(browse) the filter answered the current text and found matches - the FIRST match is selected, the RHS takes focus', '[filtered](*::server:query-editor:filtered)']
  - ['`enter`', '(pick) the filter answered with a match - the query REDUCES to the first match''s path; the host takes the commit', '[idle_path](*::server:query-editor:idle_path)']
  - ['`enter`', '(pick) the filter answered with NOTHING and the host TAKES the miss (a verbatim parseable pointer, or a create-on-miss-eligible bare name) - null commits; the host decides', '[idle_path](*::server:query-editor:idle_path)']
  - ['`enter`', '(pick) the filter answered with NOTHING and the host cannot take the miss - the typed query STAYS in the cells for correction; never a modal error', '[error_ring](*::server:query-editor:error_ring)']
  - ['`enter`', '(browse) the filter answered and found nothing', '[nop](*::server:query-editor:nop)']
  - ['`enter`', 'the filter is still in flight - the Enter is remembered and commits on arrival', '`cell_editing` (stays)']
  - ['`enter`', 'the query does not parse', '[error_ring](*::server:query-editor:error_ring)']
  - ['`escape`', '', '[idle_path](*::server:query-editor:idle_path)']
  - ['`click_outside`', '', '[idle_path](*::server:query-editor:idle_path)']
  - ['`evicted`', '', '[idle_path](*::server:query-editor:idle_path)']
  - ['`toc_click`', '(pick) the cells BECOME the clicked node''s spelling in the current scope, caret at the end - editing continues, a click never commits', '`cell_editing` (stays)']
  - ['`toc_click`', '(browse) the clicked row is a MATCH of the query - the query is kept', '[filtered](*::server:query-editor:filtered)']
  - ['`toc_click`', '(browse) otherwise - the breadcrumb regresses to the clicked node''s plain path', '[idle_path](*::server:query-editor:idle_path)']
